.\docs\evidence\index.html:1:<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>meta-harness — evidence bundle (raw captures)</title><style>body{font:15px/1.5 system-ui,Segoe UI,Arial,sans-serif;max-width:64rem;margin:2rem auto;padding:0 1rem;color:#12232e}code{background:#f1f3f5;padding:0 .2em;word-break:break-all}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%}td,th{border-top:1px solid #ddd;padding:.4em .5em;vertical-align:top;text-align:left}.note{border-left:4px solid #b45309;padding:.5em 1em;background:#fffbeb}.sha{font-size:.85em}</style></head><body><h1>Evidence bundle — raw captures, served as committed</h1><p class="note"><strong>Nothing here is generated or prettified except the index pages.</strong> Every capture is served byte-for-byte as committed under <code>docs/evidence/</code>; each directory's index lists every capture with its full URL, what it proves, and the SHA-256 of the committed bytes. The deploy that placed these files recorded the same digests in the production record.</p><h2>Start here</h2><p>The single finding most worth verifying first: on 2026-09-13, commit 109053ad failed its CI verification (step &#x27;Unit tests&#x27;) and GitHub&#x27;s automatic legacy Pages build deployed that same commit anyway. The capture below is the API read-back taken on 2026-09-14 before anything was changed; VERIFY-COLD.md gives the anonymous API calls and expected values so it can be re-checked without us.<br><code>https://mahmood726-cyber.github.io/meta-harness/evidence/gate-authority-2026-09-14/01-prefix-deploy-unconditional.txt</code></p><h2>Directories</h2><ul><li><a href="artifact-identity-2026-09-14/">Artifact identity (2026-09-14): build once, verify that artifact, deploy exactly it, fetch it back</a> — The first gated deploy re-tarred an artifact verify had never seen. These captures show that defect from the run logs, the second-path sweep, what could not be closed, and the first chained deploy. (5 captures) <br><code>https://mahmood726-cyber.github.io/meta-harness/evidence/artifact-identity-2026-09-14/</code></li><li><a href="comparator-correctness-2026-09-15/">Comparator correctness (2026-09-15): symmetric external findings with verification NONE</a> — Lane AE evidence comparing forest-plot-only comparator effect inputs and parsed characteristics tables with the repository pools under the same correctness instrument. (23 captures) <br><code>https://mahmood726-cyber.github.io/meta-harness/evidence/comparator-correctness-2026-09-15/</code></li><li><a href="decoupling-universal-2026-09-15/">Diagnostic-decision decoupling was universal (2026-09-15): 32 of 32 topics routed a detected hazard to the reader instead of a decision</a> — The headline finding behind the crystalloids instance: before any consumer was wired, every one of the 32 reviews carried at least one detected, rendered hazard connected to no analytic decision. Generated from the pre-wiring sweep; each pair&#x27;s fate (wired / informational / owed) is named. (2 captures) <br><code>https://mahmood726-cyber.github.io/meta-harness/evidence/decoupling-universal-2026-09-15/</code></li><li><a href="deploy-target-2026-09-15/">Deploy target (2026-09-15): 14 consecutive main deploys failed before any check ran; verify green, site stale at 34747bd6</a> — Since d15867aa (2026-09-14 22:22Z) the checkout-free deploy job ran scripts/production_record.py without the harness package it imports and died on ModuleNotFoundError before checking anything; with the package shipped it would have died on `ref not resolvable: HEAD` because there is no repository in the job. Every landing since -- including the search benchmark and search_v2 -- is on GitHub and NOT live. The deploy job now names its target from the manifest it was handed (commit_sha as head, the manifest digest as tree) and still refuses a tampered artifact. (2 captures) <br><code>https://mahmood726-cyber.github.io/meta-harness/evidence/deploy-target-2026-09-15/</code></li><li><a href="design-key-2026-09-14/">Design key (2026-09-14): typed actions and evidence-backed correlation handling</a> — This tranche stamps every pooled trial with a canonical design key, maps detected hazards to typed actions, replaces the trusted correlation boolean with evidence-backed provenance, states non-parallel prevalence as UNKNOWN, and rebuilds all 32 live review pages. (13 captures) <br><code>https://mahmood726-cyber.github.io/meta-harness/evidence/design-key-2026-09-14/</code></li><li><a href="fix-ladder-2026-09-14/">Fix ladder applied to the 40 existing fix claims (2026-09-14)</a> — Codex lane J, a non-author, tried to re-demonstrate each of the 40 entries in docs/fix_ledger.json from served bytes or committed objects; 28 REPRODUCED (proposed VERIFIED), 12 name a mechanism or artefact that does not exist in the tree (proposed REPORTED). (42 captures) <br><code>https://mahmood726-cyber.github.io/meta-harness/evidence/fix-ladder-2026-09-14/</code></li><li><a href="fixstate-orthogonal-2026-09-14/">Fix-state orthogonal schema (2026-09-14): four fields plus computed freshness</a> — Lane AA evidence for replacing the ladder with implementation, verification, scope and computed freshness, plus sealed gate-gap rows. (5 captures) <br><code>https://mahmood726-cyber.github.io/meta-harness/evidence/fixstate-orthogonal-2026-09-14/</code></li><li><a href="gate-authority-2026-09-14/">Gate authority (2026-09-14): deploy conditional on verification; server-side rule; one standard</a> — Before this tranche a commit that failed CI was served (109053ad). These captures show the pre-fix state from the API, the refusals after the fix, and the clean cases. (13 captures) <br><code>https://mahmood726-cyber.github.io/meta-harness/evidence/gate-authority-2026-09-14/</code></li><li><a href="hazard-consumers-2026-09-14/">Hazard consumers (2026-09-14): limitation hazards wired to executable gates or acknowledged as unwired</a> — This bundle records the lane AD sweep for diagnostic-decision decoupling: every limitation object has a consumer edge or an explicit unwired acknowledgement, with plants for each wired mapping. (5 captures) <br><code>https://mahmood726-cyber.github.io/meta-harness/evidence/hazard-consumers-2026-09-14/</code></li><li><a href="identifier-scope-2026-09-14/">Identifier-scope detector (2026-09-14): single-agent identifier over class-level pool</a> — Lane Y evidence: a structural detector marks the spironolactone identifier as too narrow for a mixed spironolactone/eplerenone MRA pool while leaving the identifier itself unchanged. (5 captures) <br><code>https://mahmood726-cyber.github.io/meta-harness/evidence/identifier-scope-2026-09-14/</code></li><li><a href="independent-verification-2-2026-09-14/">Independent re-demonstration 2 (2026-09-14): lane R re-run of ladder claims</a> — Codex (GPT-5), lane R, not the author of the fixes, re-ran the fix-state, scorecard, legacy-ledger, evidence-index, override-audit, prospective-control, and architecture-identity claims from a fresh clone and the served site. (8 captures) <br><code>https://mahmood726-cyber.github.io/meta-harness/evidence/independent-verification-2-2026-09-14/</code></li><li><a href="independent-verification-2026-09-14/">Independent re-demonstration (2026-09-14): eleven claims re-performed by a non-author agent from a fresh clone</a> — Codex (GPT-5), not the author of any fix, re-ran every claim from a fresh clone with raw commands and outputs. 9 REPRODUCED, 2 COULD NOT TEST (no token in that sandbox). (12 captures) <br><code>https://mahmood726-cyber.github.io/meta-harness/evidence/independent-verification-2026-09-14/</code></li><li><a href="legacy-ledgers-2026-09-14/">Legacy ledgers for the 32 pre-ledger topics; raw external inputs preserved (2026-09-14)</a> — The 32 committed caches predate the retrieval ledger. Each now carries an explicit LEGACY_UNRECORDED ledger and the pages render it. (2 captures) <br><code>https://mahmood726-cyber.github.io/meta-harness/evidence/legacy-ledgers-2026-09-14/</code></li><li><a href="limitation-softening-read-2026-09-14/">Limitation softening read (2026-09-14): absent/banner block pairs before structured objects</a> — One-time model-read audit of whether absent/banner limitation blocks were softened across regenerations b8925e04 and f928a536; superseded by the limitations-as-objects design. (33 captures) <br><code>https://mahmood726-cyber.github.io/meta-harness/evidence/limitation-softening-read-2026-09-14/</code></li><li><a href="limitations-objects-2026-09-14/">Limitations as structured objects (2026-09-14): object layer plus legacy comparison</a> — Lane W stage 1-2 evidence: review.json carries structured limitation objects, page.py remains the legacy renderer, and every legacy absent/banner block maps one-to-one to an object. (5 captures) <br><code>https://mahmood726-cyber.github.io/meta-harness/evidence/limitations-objects-2026-09-14/</code></li><li><a href="override-audit-2026-09-14/">Audit of the 23 override:true entries across 11 topics (2026-09-14)</a> — Each override: what it replaces, with what, the stated reason, whether its source is committed, and whether it encodes a rule the harness should carry generally (grouped candidates) or a one-off fact. (2 captures) <br><code>https://mahmood726-cyber.github.io/meta-harness/evidence/override-audit-2026-09-14/</code></li><li><a href="probiotics-search-diagnostic-2026-09-15/">Probiotics AAD search diagnostic (2026-09-15): Goodman 42, our funnel, reachability and cap accounting</a> — Comparator-to-object diagnostic for the probiotics AAD topic: Goodman 2021&#x27;s 42 named trials, the committed 468-record screening funnel, the comparator rows not pooled by us, and dated PubMed/CT.gov reachability measurements. (6 captures) <br><code>https://mahmood726-cyber.github.io/meta-harness/evidence/probiotics-search-diagnostic-2026-09-15/</code></li><li><a href="query-structure-2026-09-14/">Query structure classification, 32 topics named (2026-09-14)</a> — Structural reclassification of every committed retrieval query in the 32 live pages, with fired features and page-level retraction checks. (2 captures) <br><code>https://mahmood726-cyber.github.io/meta-harness/evidence/query-structure-2026-09-14/</code></li><li><a href="ratchet-blocks-2026-09-14/">Ratchet block accounting (2026-09-14): phrase counts missed 15 lost honest-state blocks</a> — The phrase-only honest-state ratchet saw zero violations at b8925e04, but block-level absent/banner tracking reports 15 lost blocks and names the affected pages. (2 captures) <br><code>https://mahmood726-cyber.github.io/meta-harness/evidence/ratchet-blocks-2026-09-14/</code></li><li><a href="regeneration-accounting-2026-09-14/">Regeneration byte accounting, 32 topics named (2026-09-14)</a> — Every hunk of both page regenerations (b8925e04 retrieval-class states; f928a536 legacy ledgers) classified per topic as intended provenance, incidental, or a LOST honest state. Finding: 15 topics lost the old &#x27;Search provenance&#x27; absent-block (with its explicit retraction sentence) in the first regeneration; the ratchet did not catch it because it counts phrases, not blocks. The first pass looked at the wrong commit and reported 0/0/0 -- recorded, not hidden. (33 captures) <br><code>https://mahmood726-cyber.github.io/meta-harness/evidence/regeneration-accounting-2026-09-14/</code></li><li><a href="scorecard-adjudication-2026-09-14/">Scorecard adjudication (2026-09-14): events carry adjudication objects</a> — Schema v2 correction for the gate scorecard: precision is computed from adjudication objects and reported only beside coverage; unresolved refusals are neither TP nor FP. (4 captures) <br><code>https://mahmood726-cyber.github.io/meta-harness/evidence/scorecard-adjudication-2026-09-14/</code></li><li><a href="search-acquisition-2026-09-14/">Acquisition layer (2026-09-14): retrieval ledger, run states, pagination, concept source, regression-corpus recall</a> — Nothing recorded how a record was found. These captures show the old fetch&#x27;s defects offline, the plants, a live refresh with full provenance, and the recall measurement. (8 captures) <br><code>https://mahmood726-cyber.github.io/meta-harness/evidence/search-acquisition-2026-09-14/</code></li><li><a href="search-benchmark-2026-09-15/">Search benchmark (2026-09-15): labelled known positives and sealed dev/measurement split</a> — Lane S1 evidence: every known-positive trial named by source, deterministic 11/21 split, and an offline scorer plant with refusals. (4 captures) <br><code>https://mahmood726-cyber.github.io/meta-harness/evidence/search-benchmark-2026-09-15/</code></li><li><a href="search-benchmark-identifiers-2026-09-15/">Identifiers proposed for the 20 identifier-less benchmark positives (2026-09-15): Codex lane R3; the sealed benchmark is NOT edited</a> — 20 benchmark positives carry no PMID/NCT/DOI (11 of the 12 audit-found positives on the MEASUREMENT split among them), so the title scorer cannot match them for any engine. A Codex (gpt-5.5) lane resolved identifiers from saved PubMed / Europe PMC / CT.gov responses: RESOLVED 15 of 20, AMBIGUOUS 1 (the colchicine-postop-af &#x27;five audit-named trials&#x27; placeholder), UNRESOLVED 4 (El-Ghamrawy; Helps 2015, Iamharit 2010, Khanal 2015 -- probiotics journals not indexed). Integrator check: 15 of 15 resolved identifiers appear verbatim in the saved responses (outputs/search_v2/lanes/R3/lane_r3/raw/, 178 files) and 16 of 16 in_r2_candidates claims match the candidate file. Of the 11 MEASUREMENT audit positives, 6 (Mikami, Snijders, SONIA, EMPA-VISION, IRON-HF, Toblli 2007) are in the run-r2 candidate set. Adopting these is a benchmark re-seal event and is not done here. (2 captures) <br><code>https://mahmood726-cyber.github.io/meta-harness/evidence/search-benchmark-identifiers-2026-09-15/</code></li><li><a href="search-provenance-restored-2026-09-14/">Search provenance restored from the retrieval-class object (2026-09-14)</a> — The lost Search provenance absent block is restored on all 32 review pages from search.retrieval_class.search_provenance, with the fifteen accounting losses compared word by word. (6 captures) <br><code>https://mahmood726-cyber.github.io/meta-harness/evidence/search-provenance-restored-2026-09-14/</code></li><li><a href="search-states-2026-09-14/">Retrieval class as an object state (2026-09-14): two rendered states on all 32 pages; the honest-state ratchet</a> — Pages rendered a hedge read from a side file. These captures show that, the regeneration proof, the states now served, and the ratchet refusing a lost honest state. (5 captures) <br><code>https://mahmood726-cyber.github.io/meta-harness/evidence/search-states-2026-09-14/</code></li><li><a href="search-v2-2026-09-15/">search_v2 engine, development run (2026-09-15): P/I/C queries, three sources cross-linked, citation chasing, no truncation, replayable snapshots</a> — Lane S2 built the search capability and ran it on the 11 DEVELOPMENT topics only. No recall number is claimed here: development topics are a fit statistic, not capability; the measurement lane scores the 21 MEASUREMENT topics against targets the engine&#x27;s developer never saw. (5 captures) <br><code>https://mahmood726-cyber.github.io/meta-harness/evidence/search-v2-2026-09-15/</code></li><li><a href="search-v2-guard-2026-09-15/">search_v2 query guard (2026-09-15): RETROSPECTIVE protocol for the sealed-vocabulary exemption, with plants fired before and after</a> — 5 of 21 sealed MEASUREMENT topics were RAN_ERROR because the engine&#x27;s anti-name-seeding guard refused a registered vocabulary token that is not a trial name (CABG, BAY94-8862, PCSK9, LCZ696, NSTE-ACS). The rule that replaces the hand-grown allowlist is stated here in full, labelled retrospective, with both answers it yields disclosed before the re-run; the plants show the detector still fires. (4 captures) <br><code>https://mahmood726-cyber.github.io/meta-harness/evidence/search-v2-guard-2026-09-15/</code></li><li><a href="search-v2-independent-2026-09-15/">Independent re-demonstration of the search_v2 claims (2026-09-15): Codex lane R1, fresh clone, adversarial brief</a> — A Codex (gpt-5.5) lane at f62eec27 was briefed to BREAK five claims of the session author: the pre-fix plants, the run-r2 recall, the raw-archive custody, the register on search_v2, and the completeness gate. It reproduced all five with its own probes and its own PMID/NCT-only scorer. Its sandbox could not create git worktrees (it used git archive of 01e39f2e) and had no gh credentials (it used urllib against the release API). It also ran Stop-Process on a shell it mistook for its own -- recorded here, and every later brief forbids it. (9 captures) <br><code>https://mahmood726-cyber.github.io/meta-harness/evidence/search-v2-independent-2026-09-15/</code></li><li><a href="search-v2-measurement-2026-09-15/">search_v2 measurement (2026-09-15): sealed 21-topic recall, two runs beside each other, routes, misses, register on search_v2, 32-topic before/after</a> — Run 1 (lane S3): the frozen engine on the sealed MEASUREMENT topics, 5 of 21 RAN_ERROR (guard refused vocabulary). Run r2: the same benchmark after the guard protocol, one engine blob on all 32 topics, states counted separately, the sealed register measured on search_v2 within kind, the pinned legacy cache compared with the new snapshots. Run r3 (Codex lane R4): engine v3 = r2 + the ISRCTN registry adapter, again all 32 topics. No run replaces another; served pages were not moved. (19 captures) <br><code>https://mahmood726-cyber.github.io/meta-harness/evidence/search-v2-measurement-2026-09-15/</code></li><li><a href="search-v2-verification-2026-09-15/">Source verification of run r2&#x27;s new automated includes (2026-09-15): 32 Codex lanes + 4 remainder lanes + a blind second opinion, adjudicated mechanically</a> — Per-topic Codex lanes gave every NEW r2 include a quoted verdict against the protocol PICO; the integrator re-derived every N from committed artefacts and never read lane prose. MEASUREMENT totals: 21 of 21 topics harvested, 6 of 21 clean; NEW 1998; ELIGIBLE_RCT 27 of 1998; ELIGIBLE_RCT_NO_PRIMARY 397; NOT_RCT 489; WRONG_* 288; DUPLICATE 255; UNDECIDABLE 53; NOT_VERIFIED_CAP 0; REGISTRY_ONLY 482; automated screen agreed 424 of 1998 A blind second lane upheld 19 of 39 first-lane ELIGIBLE_RCT rows. No pool moved. (4 captures) <br><code>https://mahmood726-cyber.github.io/meta-harness/evidence/search-v2-verification-2026-09-15/</code></li><li><a href="target-assertion-2026-09-14/">Target assertion (2026-09-14): every check names its target or refuses</a> — The phrase-ratchet accounting pass demonstrated why silent target defaults are unsafe: the first pass looked at the wrong commit and reported zeros. These captures show prefix silence, postfix TARGET lines, planted refusals, and the ratchet fix-state downgrade. (5 captures) <br><code>https://mahmood726-cyber.github.io/meta-harness/evidence/target-assertion-2026-09-14/</code></li></ul><h2>Verify the bytes you are reading</h2><p>This site is deployed only by the deploy job of .github/workflows/verify.yml, which consumes the artifact the verify job produced and fetches every file back. The per-file SHA-256 manifest of the deployed tree is served at https://mahmood726-cyber.github.io/meta-harness/_production/manifest.json (key files[&#x27;evidence/&lt;dir&gt;/&lt;file&gt;&#x27;]). The post-deploy attestation record for each deployment is at https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mahmood726-cyber/meta-harness/production-records/&lt;full commit sha&gt;.json. Each directory index below also prints the SHA-256 of every capture&#x27;s committed bytes.</p><h2>If github.com refuses you, try these hosts (same bytes)</h2><ul><li>Raw content host (the 109053ad capture): <code>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/mahmood726-cyber/meta-harness/main/docs/evidence/gate-authority-2026-0