C:\meta-harness\outputs\search_v2\verification\tocilizumab-covid19-mortality\lane.log:376:  "evidence_base_caveat": "Evidence base incomplete and NOT a field-representative meta-analysis. Only one trial (RECOVERY, PMID 33933206) is pooled for 28-day mortality here, because the other trial abstracts in this corpus did not yield extractable per-arm counts. The comprehensive comparator (WHO REACT, PMID 34228774, JAMA 2021) pools ~27 trials and reports OR 0.86 (0.79-0.95). A post-fix full-text pass this cycle source-verified 28-day mortality counts for five further eligible RCTs (REMDACTA 34609549, COVACTA 33631066, EMPACTA 33332779, BACC Bay 33085857, Salvarani 33472855) -- but they were deliberately NOT pooled: adding those five small/early-era trials WITHOUT the large trials still missing from this corpus (notably REMAP-CAP, not present here) yields a biased 6-of-~27 subset whose pooled OR (0.98, null) is an artifact of partial completion that diverges from the comprehensive comparator. Completing this topic requires a proper search rebuild to the full trial set, not a partial extraction; the verified counts are held pending that.",
C:\meta-harness\outputs\search_v2\verification\tocilizumab-covid19-mortality\lane.log:2101:  "evidence_base_caveat": "Evidence base incomplete and NOT a field-representative meta-analysis. Only one trial (RECOVERY, PMID 33933206) is pooled for 28-day mortality here, because the other trial abstracts in this corpus did not yield extractable per-arm counts. The comprehensive comparator (WHO REACT, PMID 34228774, JAMA 2021) pools ~27 trials and reports OR 0.86 (0.79-0.95). A post-fix full-text pass this cycle source-verified 28-day mortality counts for five further eligible RCTs (REMDACTA 34609549, COVACTA 33631066, EMPACTA 33332779, BACC Bay 33085857, Salvarani 33472855) -- but they were deliberately NOT pooled: adding those five small/early-era trials WITHOUT the large trials still missing from this corpus (notably REMAP-CAP, not present here) yields a biased 6-of-~27 subset whose pooled OR (0.98, null) is an artifact of partial completion that diverges from the comprehensive comparator. Completing this topic requires a proper search rebuild to the full trial set, not a partial extraction; the verified counts are held pending that.",
