The adjudicator script’s expected-denominator logic accounts only the primary outcome’s pooled and declared-absent trial identifiers. I’m narrowing the shared-NCT check to that same primary-outcome basis so the omission classification matches the denominator machinery.
exec
"C:\\WINDOWS\\System32\\WindowsPowerShell\\v1.0\\powershell.exe" -Command '$env:PYTHONIOENCODING='"'utf-8'; @'
import json,re
from pathlib import Path
om=json.loads(Path(r'C:/meta-harness/outputs/search_v2/verification/omitted_rows.json').read_text(encoding='utf-8'))
def primary_matches(slug,nct):
